σινδών, -όνος, ἡ 
 [in LXX: Jdg.14:12-13 A, Pro.31:24 (סָדִין), 1Ma.10:64 A * ;] 
fine linen cloth; 
 __(a) as used for swathing dead bodies (cf. Hdt., ii, 86): Mat.27:59, Mrk.15:46, Luk.23:53; 
 __(b) a garment or wrap of this material (cf. ICC, Jg, l.with): Mrk.14:51-52.†
 (AS)

A man living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Sa.1.3; 
 son of: Eli (H5941); 
 brother of: Hophni (H2652); 
 father of: Ichabod (H0350), Ahitub (H0285)
 § Phinehas = "mouth of brass"
1) son of Eleazar and grandson of Aaron; his zealousness for the Lord averted a plague on Israel and gained him the promise of the Lord of an everlasting priesthood in his family
2) a priest and the son of the priest Eli
3) the father of a helper of Ezra

A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Divided Monarchy, only mentioned at 1Ch.4.7; 
 son of: Ashhur (H0806) and Helah (H2458); 
 brother of: Haahashtari (H0326), Izhar (H3328), Ethnan (H0869) and Koz (H6976); 
 half-brother of: Ahuzzam (H0275), Hepher (H2660) and Temeni (H8488) 
 § Zereth = "splendour"
 son of Ashur, the founder of Tekoa, by his wife Helah
